# Jak 3, 0.1.8 (LIST-0.1.8 item 6, Steer by grabbing the wheel; the owner: "look over all the vehicles to be sure
# gripping whatever wheel/control type they have works"): the vehicles Jak 3's ride kinds leave out, each by its own
# continue with JAKVR_STATE_TRACE=1: JAKVR_TEST_CONTINUE=hanga-start (the glider: its bar), comba-sled (the
# catacombs' sled), factoryb-start (the war factory's hellcat: a race continue seating him in it; factoryd-start,
# tried first, is the Titan suit). The opening skipped and a new game started as jak3_buggy.sim does, the continue
# taken once Jak is first in play; once he sits (counted from that frame, below) A held (Cross: the throttle where
# there is one), both grips squeezed where the hands rest, turned to the right as a wheel (the right down, the left up),
# back, to the left as handlebars (the right pushed ahead, the left pulled back), back, let go. Expect "[vr-pad] the
# wheel held by ..." (the glider: "handlebars or a bar"; the sled and the hellcat: "a wheel"), "[vr-pad] the
# wheel: turned ... steering ..." lines and the vehicle turning in the pictures; none where he pilots nothing yet.
# 0.1.8 (sims rw3g and rw3s, builds 101 to 103): the continues seat Jak at a frame that varies from run to run (about
# 4750 on the glider, later on the sled), so fixed frames missed him (the grips squeezed before he sat held nothing, as
# they should). Build 104 on: run with QUEST_SIM_ALIGN=10000. The lines from 10000 count from the frame the continue
# seats him (pc-vr.gc vr-test-continue!, "[vr] test: seated by the continue, the set-up done"), the driving 60 frames
# after it.
